  green: [['50','#f0fdf4','#0f172a'],['100','#dcfce7','#0f172a'],['200','#bbf7d0','#0f172a'],['300','#86efac','#0f172a'],['400','#4ade80','#0f172a'],['500','#22c55e','#0f172a'],['600','#16a34a','#0f172a'],['700','#15803d','#ffffff'],['800','#166534','#ffffff'],['900','#14532d','#ffffff'],['950','#052e16','#ffffff']],
  amber: [['50','#fffbeb','#0f172a'],['100','#fef3c7','#0f172a'],['200','#fde68a','#0f172a'],['300','#fcd34d','#0f172a'],['400','#fbbf24','#0f172a'],['500','#f59e0b','#0f172a'],['600','#d97706','#0f172a'],['700','#b45309','#ffffff'],['800','#92400e','#ffffff'],['900','#78350f','#ffffff'],['950','#451a03','#ffffff']],
  red: [['50','#fef2f2','#0f172a'],['100','#fee2e2','#0f172a'],['200','#fecaca','#0f172a'],['300','#fca5a5','#0f172a'],['400','#f87171','#0f172a'],['500','#ef4444','#0f172a'],['600','#dc2626','#ffffff'],['700','#b91c1c','#ffffff'],['800','#991b1b','#ffffff'],['900','#7f1d1d','#ffffff'],['950','#450a0a','#ffffff']],
  blue: [['50','#eff6ff','#0f172a'],['100','#dbeafe','#0f172a'],['200','#bfdbfe','#0f172a'],['300','#93c5fd','#0f172a'],['400','#60a5fa','#0f172a'],['500','#3b82f6','#0f172a'],['600','#2563eb','#ffffff'],['700','#1d4ed8','#ffffff'],['800','#1e40af','#ffffff'],['900','#1e3a8a','#ffffff'],['950','#172554','#ffffff']],
};
---
<BaseLayout title={page.title} description={page.summary} path={page.path}>

<div class="token-ref-header">
  <div class="tr-hero">
    <p class="tr-hero-eyebrow">Foundations / Tokens</p>
    <h1>Every design decision, named once</h1>
    <p>
      A token is the smallest unit of the language: <strong>one color, one step of space, one shadow</strong>, authored as data and published to CSS and TypeScript from a single source. This is the canonical list of all {tokenCount}, and the two-tier system that generates them. Click any token to copy its <span class="tr-hero-code">var(...)</span> reference.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="toc">
    <a href="#architecture">Architecture</a>
    <a href="#primitives">Primitives</a>
    <a href="#semantic-color">Semantic color</a>
    <a href="#spacing">Spacing</a>
    <a href="#radius">Radius</a>
    <a href="#shadow">Shadow</a>
    <a href="#state">State</a>
    <a href="#typography">Typography</a>
    <a href="#motion">Motion</a>
    <a href="#z-index">Z-index</a>
    <a href="#breakpoints">Breakpoints</a>
    <a href="#taxonomy">Taxonomy rules</a>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="quick-ref">
  <div class="quick-ref-item">
    <div class="quick-ref-value">{tokenCount}</div>
    <div class="quick-ref-label">Total Tokens</div>
  </div>
  <div class="quick-ref-item">
    <div class="quick-ref-value">2</div>
    <div class="quick-ref-label">Tiers</div>
  </div>
  <div class="quick-ref-item">
    <div class="quick-ref-value">8</div>
    <div class="quick-ref-label">Radius Steps</div>
  </div>
  <div class="quick-ref-item">
    <div class="quick-ref-value">3</div>
    <div class="quick-ref-label">Elevation Shadows</div>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="token-ref-section" id="architecture">
  <h2 class="token-ref-section-title"><Icon name="account_tree" /> Tokens as a Contract</h2>
  <p class="token-ref-lede">
    Every token is authored as data, not CSS, in the W3C Design Tokens Community Group format: a JSON object with a reserved <code>$value</code> and a <code>$type</code> like <code>color</code> or <code>dimension</code>. One authored decision publishes to CSS, TypeScript, and native from the same source. The JSON is the contract, and everything downstream honors it. It runs in two tiers.
  </p>

  <div class="tier-grid">
    <div class="arch-card">
      <span class="arch-card-badge">Tier 1</span>
      <div class="arch-card-title">Primitive</div>
      <p class="arch-card-text">
        The raw palette. Eight color ramps of eleven shades each, plus pure white and black. These carry a value and nothing else, no role, no meaning. Product code rarely touches this tier directly. It exists so the semantic tier has something concrete to point at. Naming is descriptive: <code>--color-indigo-600</code>.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="arch-card">
      <span class="arch-card-badge">Tier 2</span>
      <div class="arch-card-title">Semantic</div>
      <p class="arch-card-text">
        The layer you build with. Each token names a role, not a hue, and aliases a primitive: <code>--color-primary</code>, <code>--color-text-body</code>, <code>--color-border</code>. This indirection is what makes the system themeable. Change one alias, and every consumer moves with it. Naming is intentional: role first, variant second.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <p class="token-ref-lede" style={{ 'margin-top': '1.5rem' }}>
    Style Dictionary reads that JSON, resolves the aliases, and formats each target. The CSS output is a flat block of custom properties on <code>:root</code>, a parallel TypeScript output exposes the same values as typed constants. Both carry a do-not-edit banner: they are build output, not source.
  </p>

  <div class="pipeline">
    <div class="pipeline-stage">
      <div class="pipeline-kicker">Source</div>
      <div class="pipeline-title">JSON tokens</div>
      <p class="pipeline-text">Authored by hand in DTCG format under <code>packages/tokens/src/tokens/</code>. One file per category, each token a <code>$value</code> plus a <code>$type</code>.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="pipeline-arrow">&#8594;</div>
    <div class="pipeline-stage">
      <div class="pipeline-kicker">Build</div>
      <div class="pipeline-title">Style Dictionary</div>
      <p class="pipeline-text">Resolves aliases, applies transforms, and formats each platform target. Run once, every output stays in lockstep.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="pipeline-arrow">&#8594;</div>
    <div class="pipeline-stage">
      <div class="pipeline-kicker">Generated</div>
      <div class="pipeline-title">CSS and TS</div>
      <p class="pipeline-text"><code>dist/tokens.css</code> as <code>:root</code> custom properties, <code>dist/tokens.ts</code> as typed constants. Do not edit, they are regenerated.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="token-ref-section" id="primitives">
  <h2 class="token-ref-section-title"><Icon name="palette" /> Tier 1: Primitive Palette</h2>
  <p class="token-ref-lede">
    The raw material. Indigo, slate and violet are Tailwind CSS’s open-source (MIT) default ramps, adopted hex-for-hex; ink, jade, honey, crimson and cerulean are this system’s own, authored in OKLCH so the status hues share one lightness with the brand (the Harmonic palette, see docs/research/status-tones-2026.md). Indigo is the brand ramp and the single action accent. Slate carries text, surfaces and borders; ink is the indigo-tinted neutral behind the neutral tone. Jade, honey, crimson and cerulean feed success, warning, error and info. Violet backs the secondary role, a decorative accent only, never for action. Emerald, green, amber, red and blue are deprecated: still published so nothing breaks, used by no role, and removed in a future major. Click any shade to copy its variable.
  </p>

  {[...ACTIVE, ...DEPRECATED].map((name) => (
    <div class="palette-block">
      <div class="palette-head">
        <span class="palette-name">{name}{DEPRECATED.includes(name) && <span class="palette-deprecated"> · deprecated</span>}</span>
        <code class="palette-pattern">--color-{name}-50 … 950</code>
      </div>
      <div class="palette-strip">
        {ramps[name].map(([shade, hex, fg]) => {
          return (
            <button
              class="swatch"
              data-token={`--color-${name}-${shade}`}
              style={{ background: hex, color: fg, border: shade === '50' ? '1px solid #e2e8f0' : 'none' }}
            >
              <span class="swatch-shade">{shade}</span>
              <span class="swatch-hex">{hex}</span>
            </button>
          );
        })}
      </div>
    </div>
  ))}

  <div class="tbl-scroll" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Scrollable table"><table class="token-table" style={{ 'margin-top': '1.25rem' }}>
    <thead>
      <tr><th>Preview</th><th>Token</th><th>Value</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td><div class="color-dot" style={{ background: '#ffffff', border: '1px solid #e2e8f0' }}></div></td>
        <td><span class="token-name" data-token="--color-white">--color-white</span></td>
        <td><span class="token-value">#ffffff</span></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><div class="color-dot" style={{ background: '#000000' }}></div></td>
        <td><span class="token-name" data-token="--color-black">--color-black</span></td>
        <td><span class="token-value">#000000</span></td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table></div>
</div>

<div class="token-ref-section" id="semantic-color">
  <h2 class="token-ref-section-title"><Icon name="category" /> Tier 2: Semantic Color</h2>
  <p class="token-ref-lede">
    The layer product code consumes. Each token names a role and aliases a primitive. Build with these, never with raw palette shades, so a theme change stays a one-line edit at the alias.
  </p>

  <div class="two-col-layout">
    <div>
      <h3 style={{ 'font-family': "'Plus Jakarta Sans', sans-serif", 'font-size': '0.9375rem', color: '#0f172a', 'margin-top': '0.5rem', 'margin-bottom': '0.75rem' }}>Brand</h3>
      <div class="tbl-scroll" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Scrollable table"><table class="token-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Preview</th><th>Token</th><th>Value</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          {[
            ['--color-primary', '#4f46e5', 'indigo 600, the single accent'],
            ['--color-primary-light', '#6366f1', 'indigo 500, light'],
            ['--color-primary-dark', '#4338ca', 'indigo 700, dark'],
            ['--color-primary-surface', '#eef2ff', 'indigo 50, tinted fill'],
            ['--color-secondary', '#8b5cf6', 'violet 500, decorative only'],
            ['--color-secondary-light', '#a78bfa', 'violet 400, secondary light'],
            ['--color-secondary-dark', '#7c3aed', 'violet 600, secondary (dark)'],
            ['--color-secondary-surface', '#f5f3ff', 'violet 50, secondary surface'],
          ].map(([name, hex, role]) => (
            <tr>
              <td><div class="color-dot" style={{ background: hex, border: hex === '#eef2ff' || hex === '#f5f3ff' ? '1px solid #e2e8f0' : 'none' }}></div></td>
              <td><span class="token-name" data-token={name}>{name}</span></td>
              <td><span class="token-value">{hex}</span><div class="token-description">{role}</div></td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table></div>

      <h3 style={{ 'font-family': "'Plus Jakarta Sans', sans-serif", 'font-size': '0.9375rem', color: '#0f172a', 'margin-top': '2rem', 'margin-bottom': '0.75rem' }}>Text</h3>
      <div class="tbl-scroll" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Scrollable table"><table class="token-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Preview</th><th>Token</th><th>Value</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          {[
            ['--color-text-heading', '#0f172a', 'slate 900, headings'],
            ['--color-text-strong', '#1e293b', 'slate 800, emphasis'],
            ['--color-text-secondary', '#475569', 'slate 600, supporting'],
            ['--color-text-body', '#334155', 'slate 700, body copy'],
            ['--color-text-muted', '#64748b', 'slate 500, muted, the floor on white'],
            ['--color-text-disabled', '#cbd5e1', 'slate 300, disabled, exempt from 1.4.3'],
          ].map(([name, hex, role]) => (
            <tr>
              <td><div class="color-dot" style={{ background: hex }}></div></td>
              <td><span class="token-name" data-token={name}>{name}</span></td>
              <td><span class="token-value">{hex}</span><div class="token-description">{role}</div></td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table></div>

      <h3 style={{ 'font-family': "'Plus Jakarta Sans', sans-serif", 'font-size': '0.9375rem', color: '#0f172a', 'margin-top': '2rem', 'margin-bottom': '0.75rem' }}>Surface and Border</h3>
      <div class="tbl-scroll" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Scrollable table"><table class="token-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Preview</th><th>Token</th><th>Value</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          {[
            ['--color-surface', '#ffffff', 'white, cards, panels'],
            ['--color-surface-secondary', '#f8fafc', 'slate 50, sunken fill'],
            ['--color-surface-hover', '#f1f5f9', 'slate 100, hover fill'],
            ['--color-background', '#f8fafc', 'slate 50, page canvas'],
            ['--color-border', '#e2e8f0', 'slate 200, default divider'],
            ['--color-border-light', '#e2e8f0', 'slate 200, soft divider'],
            ['--color-border-subtle', '#f1f5f9', 'slate 100, hairline'],
            ['--color-focus', '#4f46e5', 'indigo 600, focus ring'],
          ].map(([name, hex, role]) => (
            <tr>
              <td><div class="color-dot" style={{ background: hex, border: '1px solid #e2e8f0' }}></div></td>
              <td><span class="token-name" data-token={name}>{name}</span></td>
              <td><span class="token-value">{hex}</span><div class="token-description">{role}</div></td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table></div>

      <div class="callout">
        <div class="callout-title">Borders are dividers, not control outlines</div>
        <div class="callout-body">
          <strong>Rule:</strong> use <code>--color-border</code> and <code>--color-border-light</code> only to separate regions, dividers, table rows, card edges. <strong>Why:</strong> both sit near 1.2:1 against the surface, below the 3:1 floor WCAG 1.4.11 requires for the boundary of an interactive control. For the visible edge of an input, select, or checkbox, reach for a token that clears 3:1, for example <code>--color-text-muted</code> at #64748b, which is 4.55:1 on white. Never let a subtle border be the only thing marking a control’s bounds.
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div>
      <h3 style={{ 'font-family': "'Plus Jakarta Sans', sans-serif", 'font-size': '0.9375rem', color: '#0f172a', 'margin-top': '0.5rem', 'margin-bottom': '0.75rem' }}>Feedback</h3>
      <div class="tbl-scroll" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Scrollable table"><table class="token-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Preview</th><th>Token</th><th>Value</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          {[
            ['--color-success', '#03734a', 'jade 500, hue'],
            ['--color-success-strong', '#006641', 'jade 600, strong'],
            ['--color-success-solid', '#03734a', 'jade 500, solid'],
